verdicts.correction:
ky 2.1.0's shouldRetry receives `ShouldRetryState = { error: Error; retryCount: number }` (distribution/types/retry.d.ts L2-11, exported from 'ky' index.d.ts L6); there is NO `request` property, so `request.method` throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined` inside shouldRetry on the first failed request of ANY method, aborting the retry with a TypeError (and it is a TS compile error). It is repairable because both error classes carry the request: HTTPError.d.ts `request: KyRequest` and NetworkError.d.ts `request: KyRequest`; ky also exports `NetworkError` (index.d.ts L15) and type guards `isHTTPError(e): e is HTTPError`, `isNetworkError(e): e is NetworkError` (index.d.ts L18; type-guards.d.ts L49, L68). Corrected body:
```ts
import { GoogleSpreadsheet } from 'google-spreadsheet';
import { isHTTPError, isNetworkError } from 'ky';
retryConfig: {
  limit: 3,
  methods: ['get', 'put', 'delete', 'post'],
  backoffLimit: 10_000,
  shouldRetry: ({ error }) => {
    if (!isHTTPError(error) && !isNetworkError(error)) return false; // unknown error types: never retry
    if (error.request.method !== 'POST') return undefined;          // GET/PUT/DELETE: ky default logic (status codes, Retry-After, network errors)
    return isHTTPError(error) && [429, 503].includes(error.response.status); // POST: only when the server rejected it; NetworkError on POST -> false
  },
}
```
Semantics verified in Ky.js L389-404 and retry.d.ts L122-131: shouldRetry runs only after the limit and `methods` checks; `true` forces, `false` prevents, `undefined` falls through to the default checks. statusCodes/afterStatusCodes may be omitted since the snippet's values equal ky's defaults. Alternative that needs no shouldRetry: keep ky's default methods (no POST) and wrap only the idempotent POSTs (loadCells, saveUpdatedCells) in an application-level retry on HTTPError 429/503.

`GetValuesRequestOptions` is not exported by the package: dist/index.d.ts L1571 (the only export statement) and src/index.ts export exactly GoogleSpreadsheet, GoogleSpreadsheetWorksheet, GoogleSpreadsheetRow, GoogleSpreadsheetCell, GoogleSpreadsheetCellErrorValue — so the import fails with 'Module "google-spreadsheet" has no exported member GetValuesRequestOptions'. Derive it from the method instead:
```ts
import type { GoogleSpreadsheetWorksheet } from 'google-spreadsheet';
type GetValuesOpts = NonNullable<Parameters<GoogleSpreadsheetWorksheet['getCellsInRange']>[1]>;
const opts = { valueRenderOption: 'UNFORMATTED_VALUE', dateTimeRenderOption: 'FORMATTED_STRING' } as GetValuesOpts;
```
The rest of the snippet is correct: method signatures at GoogleSpreadsheetWorksheet.ts L742/L750 and dist/index.d.ts L833-834; options are forwarded verbatim as ky searchParams so dateTimeRenderOption reaches the URL at runtime.

The `params` object is serialised by gaxios 7.3.x with `new URLSearchParams(opts.params)` (build/cjs/src/gaxios.js L319-323, identical in 7.3.0 and 7.3.1), which stringifies an array by joining with commas. Executed locally on Node 24: `new URLSearchParams({ranges:['Rugs!A1:Z','FX!A1:C'], valueRenderOption:'UNFORMATTED_VALUE'}).toString()` -> `ranges=Rugs%21A1%3AZ%2CFX%21A1%3AC&valueRenderOption=UNFORMATTED_VALUE` — a single `ranges` value 'Rugs!A1:Z,FX!A1:C' instead of the repeated ranges[] the API documents, so the request does not fetch two ranges (the API will reject or mis-parse the range). gaxios's `paramsSerializer` escape hatch is marked @deprecated in common.d.ts L167-170. Fix: build the query string yourself and leave `params` out:
```ts
const qs = new URLSearchParams();
for (const r of ['Rugs!A1:Z', 'FX!A1:C']) qs.append('ranges', r);
qs.set('valueRenderOption', 'UNFORMATTED_VALUE');
qs.set('dateTimeRenderOption', 'FORMATTED_STRING');
const res = await client.request<{ valueRanges: { values?: unknown[][] }[] }>({
  url: `https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/${SHEET_ID}/values:batchGet?${qs}`,
  retry: true,
  retryConfig: { retry: 3, retryDelay: 500, maxRetryDelay: 10_000, statusCodesToRetry: [[429, 429], [500, 599]] },
});
```
The retry half of the snippet is correct: `request<T>(opts: GaxiosOptions)` (oauth2client.d.ts L548), JWT extends OAuth2Client (jwtclient.js L22), requestAsync forwards opts unchanged (oauth2client.js L455-463), gaxios retry.js L18-20 requires retry/retryConfig.
